1
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,100
Shou!

2
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,100
Shou!

3
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,500
Come out, Mountain God!

4
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,500
What did you do that for?

5
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,500
It's you. Aren't you the fairy maiden
who's in charge of brewing wine?

6
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:59,500
What are you doing
on this remote land?

7
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:04,500
Mei Shouquan and I were passing by.
Why did you make trouble for us?

8
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,100
Do you want him dead?

9
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:13,500
Did he purposely come here to break gas
and ruin my territory's aura?

10
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,500
Gas?

11
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,500
Gas derives from the five cereals

12
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:23,100
If you can't even stand such a trivial
thing, how will you be an immortal?

13
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:28,500
Trivial thing? Look at my bird!
It's turned into a "bat"!

14
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,500
Indeed it stinks!

15
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:36,500
If he's offended you,
I'll apologize on his behalf

16
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:41,100
I know he didn't do it on purpose.
He just didn't want to be rude to me

17
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:48,100
Does that mean he could be rude
to me and could knock my bird out?

18
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,500
On account that we're going to the
Eastern Sea to find the furnace...

19
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:55,500
to save lives,
please spare him

20
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:59,500
Shut up! No more nonsense!
Make way!

21
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:02,500
-What are you trying to do?
-I'll teach him a lesson!

22
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,500
I dare you to do that!

23
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:07,100
Get out of my way or
I'll punish you too!

24
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,500
All right, go ahead

25
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:15,500
I'll tell the Queen Mother you abused
your powers because of a trivial matter

26
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,100
I'll fly to...

27
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,100
Don't...!

28
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:24,500
Let me revive my bird
before I settle my scores with you!

29
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,500
Shou!

30
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:32,100
Are you all right, Shou?
Wake up!

31
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:35,100
What happened, Ruyi?
How did I get here?

32
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,300
There was an earthquake

33
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:42,100
I remember something was jolting

34
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:44,500
Everything's fine now.
Let's go

35
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:50,100
What's the stink?

36
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,500
-Where are we?
-I don't know...

37
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:59,500
Sorry I didn't even
save a drop for you

38
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,500
I thought my wide knowledge...

39
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:08,500
would allow me to travel round
the world without any difficulty

40
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,500
But I was wrong

41
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:14,500
However much flair I have for literature,
I can't get us any water

42
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,500
From now on, don't treat me as
a princess anymore

43
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,500
I don't think that's a good idea

44
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:26,100
At a difficult time like this,
we should share weal and woe

45
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,300
What's the matter with you?

46
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:41,380
Nothing.
We'll share weal and woe

47
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,500
I want water!

48
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,500
I want water...

49
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:27,100
What is it?

50
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,500
A cactus

51
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:34,100
-Is it poisonous?
-We're saved!

52
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,500
What do you mean?

53
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,500
The cactus juice will
quench our thirst

54
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:47,500
How do you expect me to eat this?!

55
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,500
This is the only thing
which can save us

56
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:58,300
No doubt about it!
It's a big piece!

57
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:12,100
It's safe for drinking

58
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,500
It tastes awful

59
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,500
-What's the matter?
-The smell is horrible

60
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:31,500
Still, you must drink it.
Just imagine it's snow pear or lychee

61
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,500
Use your imagination...

62
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,500
We must be philosophical
and optimistic...

63
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:40,100
in order to overcome every obstacle
and get ourselves out of this mess

64
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:44,500
It's because I was optimistic that
I thought you could...

65
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:47,500
get me back to the Capital
on a kite

66
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:49,500
But now we're stuck here

67
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:55,500
The unexpected always happen. I didn't
anticipate the change in wind directions

68
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:02,100
You're right. The unexpected always
happen in nature as well as in life

69
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:05,100
That means we're going to die here...

70
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:10,500
Don't lose heart, Your Highness.
We mustn't think of death

71
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:14,100
Instead, we should think of
how to live on

72
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,500
Just be optimistic and philosophical

73
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:24,500
I want to be philosophical
and optimistic!

74
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,100
Try

75
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:31,100
I want to be philosophical and...

76
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:36,500
Your Highness...!

77
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:46,100
Are you all right, Your Highness?

78
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,100
Look at you!

79
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,500
-You're filthy
-So are you

80
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,500
Smells great.
Have a bite

81
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,500
I don't want it

82
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:06,500
Why? You should be thankful
to have vulture meat to eat

83
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:11,500
If you don't eat, how will you
have the energy to move on?

84
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,500
I just have no appetite!

85
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:21,100
Just imagine it's roast chicken
or barbecued duck,

86
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,100
and it'll taste good

87
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:28,500
The last time we had cactus juice,
you wanted me to use my imagination

88
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:33,500
And now you want me to do it again.
No, I won't! I'd rather starve to death!

89
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,500
You really won't eat it?

90
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:51,300
Why did you throw it away?
Even if I don't eat it, you should

91
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:57,100
I said that we'd share weal and woe.
So I'll starve with you

92
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:59,100
We'll die together

93
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:01,100
Don't push me

94
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:04,100
All right, I'll eat it

95
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,100
It doesn't taste that bad, right?

96
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:15,100
Don't disturb me. I'm trying to imagine
myself taking a full-course mutton feast

97
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,300
What's the matter?

98
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:34,300
It's stiff and stringy!
My teeth hurt!

99
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:40,300
Please bear with it and eat it up.
We need something to give us energy

100
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:47,300
Hush...
Do you feel sorry for the vulture?

101
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:54,500
It was flying in the sky,
but now it's become roast meat

102
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,500
No...

103
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:01,500
What is it then?

104
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:05,300
I feel sorry for myself...!

105
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:08,500
-I'm a princess
-Indeed you are

106
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:12,500
Yet here I am eating cactus
and vulture meat!

107
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,500
I should be living in comfort
in the palace!

108
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,500
Indeed

109
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:30,100
You have to put aside
your status as Princess

110
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:35,500
Given the state we're in,
we must try to save ourselves

111
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:39,100
I'm not someone who
can't take hardship

112
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:45,300
When I set off,
I was prepared to suffer

113
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:51,100
But I didn't expect to
end up in a desert...!

114
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,500
I miss my father...

115
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:58,500
If I don't get out of the desert,
I'll never see him again...!

116
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,500
Don't be so pessimistic

117
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:08,100
I give you my word that I'll see you
safely back to the Capital!

118
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:13,500
You give me your word?
You can't even fend for yourself

119
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:16,500
Do you think you're
some immortal reincarnated?

120
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:20,500
If you have faith, we'll make it!

121
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:26,500
There isn't a soul in the vicinity.
How can there possibly be miracles?

122
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,300
Look!

123
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,500
Look! A shooting star!

124
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:40,500
-Oh no, I'm doomed!
-What's the matter?

125
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:45,500
According to the astrologers
in the palace, a falling star means...

126
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:50,500
someone will disappear from
the surface of the earth!

127
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:52,500
That's not true!

128
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:57,100
The merchants from the western regions
told me if you make a wish...

129
00:12:57,100 --> 00:13:00,100
upon seeing a shooting star,
your wish will come true

130
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,500
-Really?
-Yes

131
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:06,100
-What are you doing?
-Making a wish!

132
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,500
But there isn't any shooting star now

133
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,300
Another one!

134
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,500
What wish did you make?

135
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:28,100
That I could have a bath.
I haven't bathed for days. I stink!

136
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:33,100
Even if I must die, I must go to the
netherworld looking neat and clean

137
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:18,100
Oh Heaven, you're really cruel

138
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,500
It's snowing heavily!

139
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,500
Your Highness...

140
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,500
-What are you doing?
-I've found something

141
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:22,500
-I'm not going
-Come on, do have a look!

142
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,500
-What is it?
-Don't you want to bathe? Come with me

143
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:32,100
Can I possibly bathe here?
Stop having me on!

144
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,100
Water!

145
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,300
Water!

146
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,500
Surprised?

147
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,500
How did you do it?

148
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:47,100
I told you - if you have faith,
we'll make it

149
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:49,500
My wish has come true!

150
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,500
Want to know where
the water came from?

151
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
While you were asleep last night,
it snowed and the snow melted in my hands

152
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:02,100
So I quickly dug a hole
to collect it

153
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:05,100
It turned into water
when the sun came out

154
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,500
You stayed up the whole night?

155
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:14,500
Never mind. I'll catch some sleep
while you bathe

156
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:18,100
Let me teach you a method.
It's called sand bath

157
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:24,100
Rub some sand on yourself
and rinse with water

158
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:31,100
This will remove all the dead skin.
Let me help you...

159
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,100
I'm going to sleep.
You bathe

160
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:28,500
No, I'm an educated man.
How can I peep at her?

161
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,500
Just this once!

162
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:39,300
No... See no evil, hear no evil,
speak no evil. What if she finds out?

163
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:43,100
Nobody's going to tell her!

164
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:53,100
No...
Only a hooligan peeps at others

165
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:59,500
Who will tell her I'm a hooligan?
Nobody, right? I worry too much!

166
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:11,300
I just can't do it!
That's why I'm running to and fro

167
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:16,500
But whatever for?
I'm young, and I'm not a saint!

168
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:36,500
I guess once we're out of the desert,
we'll reach the Eastern Sea

169
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:40,100
You mean we're nearing our destination?
That's great!

170
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:44,500
Don't rejoice too soon. This desert
stretches for a thousand li

171
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:48,100
It's scorching hot in the day
and freezing cold at night

172
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:51,100
We might die here
if we're not careful!

173
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:52,500
Are you scared?

174
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:57,500
You think too little of me.
I've been around

175
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:00,500
A small desert doesn't daunt me

176
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:03,100
Scared?

177
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:06,500
Not with you around.
I'm most scared of you

178
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:09,500
When did you become
as glib as Wu Fuqi?

179
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:13,100
Don't hit me.
Which way should we go?

180
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,500
This way

181
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:29,500
This is strange. According to the map,
we should've reached the sea

182
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:34,300
But it's nowhere in sight.
There isn't even a drop of water

183
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:39,500
Maybe the sea is just up ahead.
Let's move on

184
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:43,500
I'm afraid I might have
interpreted the map wrongly

185
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:48,100
Sorry, I didn't mean to make you
walk all the way here for nothing

186
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:51,500
I certainly hope what you said
isn't true

187
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,500
But don't worry

188
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:58,500
Having walked for so many days,
I feel I'm fitter and stronger

189
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:02,100
I can go on for another three days
and three nights!

190
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:06,500
But before we move on,
we must decide which way to go

191
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:07,500
That way?

192
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,500
Are you all right?

193
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:14,500
Yes. Don't worry about me

194
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:18,100
You're just comforting me

195
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,500
-Want some water?
-You go ahead

196
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:47,100
What a thing to find in this desert.
There are some patterns on it

197
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,500
For you, Ruyi

198
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:56,300
Why are you giving it to me?

199
00:20:56,500 --> 00:21:03,100
No reason. It's common for
a man to give a woman a gift

200
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:07,500
Since you don't want it,
I'll throw it away

201
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:12,500
I didn't say I didn't want it. Since you
mean to give it to me, I'll accept it

202
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:15,100
Thanks

203
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:21,500
-What is this?
-What? Isn't it a stone?

204
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:24,100
It's a fossil of a conch!

205
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:26,100
What's that?

206
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:29,500
-It is a fossil of a conch!
-So?

207
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:32,500
Look around for more!

208
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,500
I've found one more!

209
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:43,500
There are a lot!

210
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:51,500
I'm so dull. Being in the mortal world,
I actually forgot that I'd seen...

211
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:54,500
the Eastern Sea turn into land
three times

212
00:21:54,500 --> 00:22:00,100
This desert could very well
be where the Eastern Sea was!

213
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:03,500
What are you mumbling about?
I've found many more fossils

214
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:05,500
Shou, we're in the Eastern Sea!

215
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,500
We are? Surely not?

216
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:11,100
It's true!
We are in the Eastern Sea!

217
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:18,100
If this land didn't use to be a sea,
there wouldn't be so many conch fossils!

218
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:27,500
We've reached the Eastern Sea!

219
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:33,300
-So where's the furnace?
-Under the sand!

220
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:36,500
Let's find it then!
Which spot is it under?

221
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:38,500
I don't know!

222
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:43,100
This place is vast.
How are we going to look for it?

223
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:48,100
How will we find the furnace?

224
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:59,500
Sorry, I got carried away

225
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:02,500
What's the matter?

226
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:07,100
We've come to the edge of the east.
But the cave is still nowhere in sight

227
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:10,500
Could we have taken
the wrong way again?

228
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:15,500
It can't be. We headed east,
where the sun comes out from

229
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:17,500
This should be where the cave is

230
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:21,500
Maybe we haven't reached there yet.
Let's move on

231
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:24,500
-This way
-But it's so high!

232
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:42,100
This way?

233
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:45,500
I'm sure if we go this way,
we'll be able to get out of here

234
00:24:01,500 --> 00:24:05,500
Buns again.
I'm sick of them

235
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:08,500
Take it or leave it.
There's nothing else for you

236
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:14,500
I really miss the noodles and buns
in Ping'an Town. Oh, I'm drooling...

237
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:18,300
We don't live for the sake of eating

238
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:21,300
-Let me take a break
-Many tasks are awaiting you!

239
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:26,500
How can I think of my ideals when I'm
hungry? I have to fill my stomach first

240
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:30,500
Nobody's asking you to starve.
You at least have buns to eat

241
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:37,500
Life isn't just about buns!
I need to lie down!

242
00:24:39,100 --> 00:24:42,100
We don't live just
for the sake of eating!

243
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:46,500
People who cultivate their minds to
become immortals don't even eat buns

244
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:49,500
They only live on fruit
and spring water

245
00:24:51,500 --> 00:24:56,100
I can go without food, but I
don't want to become an immortal!

246
00:24:56,500 --> 00:25:00,500
My mother wants me to get a wife and
have children to carry on the family line

247
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:06,500
It's only right that one gets a wife!
I must get a wife!

248
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:11,500
But you're not an ordinary man.
You need to have more lofty dreams!

249
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:15,500
I am an ordinary man!
What nonsense are you talking about?

250
00:25:15,500 --> 00:25:20,500
No, you're not! You must do what
you should before you turn 30!

251
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:24,500
The thing I must do before I turn 30
is to get a wife!

252
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:26,500
Understand?

253
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:29,500
How can I make you see my point?

254
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:56,500
The wind is blowing again

255
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,500
What now?

256
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:09,500
Let's fly again

257
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:23,100
I feel I've grown up. I'm no longer
the princess living in clover

258
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:30,500
You're right. If we have faith,
we'll overcome all difficulties

259
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:34,500
I'm really happy to hear that

260
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:41,100
You know, I was actually quite
worried when we were in the desert

261
00:26:41,500 --> 00:26:45,100
I was afraid we might never
get out of it alive

262
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:50,500
But I didn't want to worry you. That
was why I said that to encourage you

263
00:26:50,500 --> 00:26:55,300
In any case,
thanks, Master Wei!

264
00:26:56,500 --> 00:27:03,500
Don't say that. Actually, you were
the one who gave me courage to move on

265
00:27:04,500 --> 00:27:09,300
We could get out of the desert
because we helped each other

266
00:27:11,500 --> 00:27:17,300
We're out of danger!
Thanks for watching over us, Heaven!

267
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:20,300
You do that too

268
00:27:22,500 --> 00:27:24,500
Thank you, Heaven!

269
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:31,500
At last, I'm seeing the Princess
back to the Capital!

270
00:27:36,500 --> 00:27:39,500
Why are there words on it?
When did you write them?

271
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,500
While you were asleep

272
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:44,500
We had no brush or ink.
How did you do it?

273
00:27:44,500 --> 00:27:48,100
Simple. I used twigs and
cactus juice to write

274
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:50,100
Aren't you smart!

275
00:27:50,500 --> 00:27:57,100
"Riding the waves, we hoist the sails
and cross the seas"

276
00:27:57,500 --> 00:28:01,500
"Eyes raised, I see the moon so bright,
Head bent, in homesickness I'm drowned"

277
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:07,100
Rise! Quick, rise!

278
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:47,100
Are you all right, Your Highness?
Let's move on

279
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:52,500
Oh no...
I think I've broken my leg

280
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:58,100
I'll have a look. There's a cave
up ahead. Let's rest inside

281
00:29:07,300 --> 00:29:12,300
Dragon on the left, tiger on the right.
This should be the place

282
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:20,500
Get up! This should be where
the legendary furnace is!

283
00:29:20,500 --> 00:29:23,500
-I want to sleep a while more!
-No!

284
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:26,500
Help! I want to sleep!

285
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:31,100
Fine! I'll look for it myself!

286
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:49,500
I can't figure it out

287
00:29:53,100 --> 00:29:55,100
What's going on?

288
00:29:55,500 --> 00:29:59,500
Shou! I'm sinking!

289
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:04,500
Come and join me in the fun!

290
00:30:08,500 --> 00:30:09,500
Ruyi!

291
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:11,500
Come on, Shou!

292
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:16,500
Don't move! This is quicksand!
Give me your hand!

293
00:30:19,500 --> 00:30:24,100
Don't exert any force
or you'll sink even faster!

294
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:27,500
Catch!

295
00:30:27,500 --> 00:30:29,500
-Why?
-I must save you!

296
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:34,100
-Why are you panicking?
-Don't let go or you'll sink and die!

297
00:30:34,500 --> 00:30:39,500
Hold on tight! Don't let go!
I almost got you!

298
00:30:47,500 --> 00:30:50,500
-You dragged me into it!
-What now?

299
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:54,100
Shou!

300
00:30:54,500 --> 00:30:58,500
Don't move! The more you move or
use force, the faster you sink!

301
00:31:02,300 --> 00:31:04,300
Never did I dream I'd die here

302
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:11,500
Before I die,
I'd like to tell you a secret

303
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:13,100
What is it?

304
00:31:13,500 --> 00:31:16,500
Though we weren't born
on the same day in the same year,

305
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:20,500
I don't want to die with you
on the same day in the same year

306
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:24,500
I'd rather die in your place!

307
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:32,500
Tell you what. You'll step on me
and climb out of the quicksand

308
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:36,100
It's better for one person to die
than two!

309
00:31:36,500 --> 00:31:38,500
I'll go down first

310
00:31:39,500 --> 00:31:41,500
I just can't go down

311
00:31:43,500 --> 00:31:45,500
We've reached the bottom!

312
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:48,500
You're right.
It's so shallow

313
00:31:50,500 --> 00:31:52,500
Great! We won't have to die!

314
00:31:55,500 --> 00:31:59,500
-But how do we get out of the sand?
-How would I know?

315
00:32:00,500 --> 00:32:02,100
Go to sleep!

316
00:32:02,500 --> 00:32:06,100
Sure! That was what I was doing
before you got me over

317
00:32:06,100 --> 00:32:09,500
Let's get some sleep before
we think of a way to get out

318
00:32:27,500 --> 00:32:31,100
Where are we?
Put me down

319
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:40,500
You'd better put me down

320
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:43,500
No. I prefer to carry you

321
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:48,500
There are some characters on the wall

322
00:32:52,500 --> 00:32:56,500
"Forbidden ground. Leave quick".
We'd better get out of here!

323
00:32:56,500 --> 00:32:58,500
This is probably a prank

324
00:33:01,500 --> 00:33:03,500
Why did you do that?

325
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:07,100
Nothing happened.
This is just to scare people off

326
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:10,500
This place is eerie.
We'd better go

327
00:33:10,500 --> 00:33:12,100
Just a minute

328
00:33:13,500 --> 00:33:15,500
What are you trying to do now?

329
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:18,100
It'd be a pity not to
write a poem on it

330
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:28,500
"A traveller returning from the world
only to roam the world again"

331
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:31,500
"Wei Delu and Princess Ruining
were here"

332
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:41,100
Let's go!
This place is going to collapse!

333
00:33:43,500 --> 00:33:46,100
I was hit!
Run!

334
00:35:16,300 --> 00:35:21,500
That's just our imagination.
It's not real

335
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:24,100
It's a mirage

336
00:35:29,500 --> 00:35:32,500
Don't believe in what you see

337
00:35:34,500 --> 00:35:36,500
Believe me

338
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:44,500
If that were a real camel,
we'd be saved

339
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:52,500
If that were a real camel,
we could eat its meat,

340
00:35:53,100 --> 00:35:56,100
and use its hide as clothes

341
00:35:57,500 --> 00:36:02,500
Most importantly, it can tell
directions and get us out of here

342
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:08,500
But that is just an illusion.
See, it's moving

343
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,500
Never mind about it

344
00:36:12,500 --> 00:36:17,500
Our illusion is coming over.
It's walking towards us

345
00:36:17,500 --> 00:36:19,300
Ignore it

346
00:36:25,500 --> 00:36:28,300
It's not real...

347
00:36:36,500 --> 00:36:39,500
Your Highness, I have a feeling...

348
00:36:40,500 --> 00:36:43,500
it's real

349
00:36:50,500 --> 00:36:53,900
The camel!
Go after it!

350
00:37:17,500 --> 00:37:20,500
Which way?

351
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:21,500
Where?

352
00:38:17,500 --> 00:38:19,500
Oh no, I think he's fallen for me!

353
00:38:20,500 --> 00:38:23,300
No! I mustn't let it happen!

354
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:29,500
She knows I fancy her.
Why does she keep me at a distance?

355
00:38:29,500 --> 00:38:31,500
Is it because she doesn't like me?

356
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:37,500
No! The Trio must attain
immortality before they turn 30

357
00:38:38,500 --> 00:38:43,100
He's going on to 30. I mustn't
let his effort go to naught!

358
00:38:45,300 --> 00:38:49,500
Mother wants me to get a wife
before I'm 30. I'm turning 30

359
00:38:49,500 --> 00:38:53,500
And my dream girl is right before me.
Why don't I grab this chance?

360
00:38:58,100 --> 00:39:00,500
Do you have something to say to me?

361
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:03,100
Indeed I do

362
00:39:04,100 --> 00:39:05,500
Say it then

363
00:39:06,500 --> 00:39:09,500
Do you notice
there are many rocks here?

364
00:39:14,500 --> 00:39:20,500
That means this is a huge mountain,
and a rocky mountain at that

365
00:39:21,500 --> 00:39:22,500
And then?

366
00:39:23,500 --> 00:39:26,500
Rocky mountains are unlike
other mountains

367
00:39:26,500 --> 00:39:29,500
Other mountains are
covered with plants

368
00:39:29,500 --> 00:39:34,100
But this mountain is bare.
Isn't it rare?

369
00:39:35,500 --> 00:39:39,500
It's indeed rare, right?
That's why I must take a closer look

370
00:39:41,300 --> 00:39:43,300
No talking during meditation!

371
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:48,300
Can I ask another question?

372
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:56,500
By meditating here, will we not be
hungry even if we go without food?

373
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:03,500
Whose stomach is rumbling?

374
00:40:04,500 --> 00:40:07,300
I told you one can't do without food

375
00:40:09,500 --> 00:40:11,500
Oh no! We must get out of here!

376
00:40:11,500 --> 00:40:14,500
-Where to?
-Into that cave!

377
00:40:14,500 --> 00:40:15,500
To eat?

378
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:38,500
Uncle, can I make a deal with you?

379
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:46,100
I'll give you my camel
in exchange for food and a bath

380
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:47,500
Sure

381
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:53,300
-Have some water
-Thanks

382
00:40:53,500 --> 00:40:57,100
-Here are the noodles
-Thanks

383
00:41:03,500 --> 00:41:07,500
Slowly.
You must've run into bandits

384
00:41:08,500 --> 00:41:12,500
It's a long story. We were on our way
to the Capital to "miansheng"...

385
00:41:12,500 --> 00:41:14,300
Miansheng?

386
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:19,300
I mean we come from Miansheng.
We were planning to go to the Capital

387
00:41:21,500 --> 00:41:27,500
Eat slowly.
Don't choke

388
00:41:32,500 --> 00:41:35,100
Aren't you fit, sir!

389
00:41:35,500 --> 00:41:37,500
Guess how old I am

390
00:41:38,500 --> 00:41:41,100
Around 60 or 70?

391
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:48,100
That was a long time ago!
I'm now 120 years old!

392
00:41:52,500 --> 00:41:53,900
Surely not?

393
00:41:54,500 --> 00:41:57,500
Where are all the young people
in your village?

394
00:41:57,500 --> 00:42:02,100
There aren't any.
The youngest is over 80 years old

395
00:42:12,500 --> 00:42:16,500
-I know you!
-Who are you?

396
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:18,500
-Come with me!
-Where to?

397
00:42:18,500 --> 00:42:20,100
Come on!

398
00:42:25,500 --> 00:42:27,100
Come on!

399
00:42:28,500 --> 00:42:30,500
You ran so fast!

400
00:42:31,500 --> 00:42:33,500
What sound was that?

401
00:42:33,500 --> 00:42:35,500
Come on, there isn't anybody around

402
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:45,500
Look! "A traveller returning from
the world only to roam the world again"

403
00:42:45,500 --> 00:42:47,500
Lower your voice!

404
00:42:47,500 --> 00:42:50,500
-Lu and the Princess were here!
-Not so loud!

405
00:42:50,500 --> 00:42:52,500
Lu might be inside.
Lu!

406
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:53,500
Shhh!

407
00:43:12,500 --> 00:43:16,100
-What is it?
-The furnace!

408
00:43:16,500 --> 00:43:18,500
That's really it?

409
00:43:19,500 --> 00:43:21,500
Open it up and see

410
00:43:38,100 --> 00:43:40,100
"Manual Of Deity Of Medicine"?

411
00:43:41,500 --> 00:43:44,500
This book has been lost for years!

412
00:43:44,500 --> 00:43:48,500
It explains, treats and cures diseases
based on the five elements

413
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:51,500
That means it can cure
all kinds of diseases?

414
00:43:51,500 --> 00:43:54,500
There's hope for the people
in Ping'an Town!

415
00:43:54,500 --> 00:43:55,500
Great!

416
00:44:04,500 --> 00:44:06,500
Is it an earthquake?

417
00:44:11,500 --> 00:44:13,100
Let's get out of here!

418
00:44:15,300 --> 00:44:16,300
Run!

419
00:44:30,500 --> 00:44:31,500
Subtitled by Transtar Media Services


